*> Real-data validation driver (feature 002, F2US1): runs the content library's loaders over the generated tree
*> the extraction tool produced and reports, per loader, the status, the elapsed time and (on standard error, in
*> order with the report lines) the loader's own ERROR lines. COBOLCRAFT_GENERATED names the generated directory
*> (default build/extract-real/generated); the driver fails loudly when the packs check does not accept it. It calls
*> CONTENT-PACKS-CHECK, CONTENT-OPEN for the standard type, then each loader on <generated>/vanilla-data (the folder
*> that holds data/). A failing loader is reported and the driver goes on; the exit status is 1 when any failed.
*> Report lines (standard error, so they interleave with the loaders' ERROR lines):
*>   LOADER <name> status=<n> <ok|FAILED> seconds=<s.cc>
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ACC-F2US1-REAL-DATA.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CONTENT.
 01 WS-GENERATED           PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-ROOT                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-REASON              PIC X(128).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SHOWN               PIC 9(4).
 01 WS-SHOWN-FAILED        PIC 9(4).
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(24).
 01 WS-FAILED              BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-TOTAL               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-FATAL               PIC X(300).
 01 WS-CLOCK.
    05 WS-CLOCK-DATE       PIC X(8).
    05 WS-CLOCK-HH         PIC 99.
    05 WS-CLOCK-MM         PIC 99.
    05 WS-CLOCK-SS         PIC 99.
    05 WS-CLOCK-CC         PIC 99.
    05 FILLER              PIC X(9).
 01 WS-START               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-END                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ELAPSED             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SECONDS             PIC Z(4)9.99.
 01 WS-NOW                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-GENERATED
     ACCEPT WS-GENERATED FROM ENVIRONMENT "COBOLCRAFT_GENERATED"
     IF WS-GENERATED = SPACES
         MOVE "build/extract-real/generated" TO WS-GENERATED
     END-IF
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-REASON
     CALL "CONTENT-PACKS-CHECK" USING WS-GENERATED WS-STATUS WS-REASON
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-SHOWN
     DISPLAY "PACKS-CHECK status=" WS-SHOWN " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-REASON) UPON STDERR
     IF WS-STATUS NOT = CT-PACKS-OK
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-FATAL
         STRING "real data: packs check status " WS-SHOWN " for "
             FUNCTION TRIM(WS-GENERATED) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-FATAL
         INSPECT WS-FATAL REPLACING FIRST "  " BY X"0000"
         CALL STATIC "cc_fatal" USING WS-FATAL
     END-IF
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO WS-STATUS
     PERFORM CLOCK-NOW
     MOVE WS-NOW TO WS-START
     MOVE 0 TO WS-ELAPSED
     CALL "CONTENT-OPEN" USING CT-TYPE-STANDARD WS-GENERATED WS-STATUS
     MOVE "CONTENT-OPEN" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM REPORT-ONE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ROOT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-GENERATED) "/vanilla-data" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-ROOT
     MOVE "RECIPES-LOAD" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CLOCK-NOW
     MOVE WS-NOW TO WS-START
     CALL "RECIPES-LOAD" USING WS-ROOT WS-STATUS
     PERFORM REPORT-ONE
     MOVE "NOISES-LOAD" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CLOCK-NOW
     MOVE WS-NOW TO WS-START
     CALL "NOISES-LOAD" USING WS-ROOT WS-STATUS
     PERFORM REPORT-ONE
     MOVE "DENSITY-FUNCTIONS-LOAD" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CLOCK-NOW
     MOVE WS-NOW TO WS-START
     CALL "DENSITY-FUNCTIONS-LOAD" USING WS-ROOT WS-STATUS
     PERFORM REPORT-ONE
     MOVE "BIOMES-LOAD" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM CLOCK-NOW
     MOVE WS-NOW TO WS-START
